From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anothers <14343424+Anothers@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 92/92] dsv41: route head/engram/dspark onto dense3 and fuse r1
 DSpark draft passes

Under r1, three dense EXL3 projections still fell through to the legacy strips
path (tensorfold_exl3_linear_v4.linear, ~2.17 ms/window across 7 calls): the
backbone LM head (K2=12), prefill engram.wkv (K2=10), and dspark.main_proj
(K2=8). Route all three onto the fused dense3 (lanes) path when their shapes
and widths are supported (chunking dspark.main_proj at dense.rows_max during
ingest), which forms-in-place converts with zero extra memory.

In addition, bring DSpark's r1 pass in line with the main decoder's fusions:
- run n <= 16 mHC boundaries directly via mhcInto instead of Triton _site;
- fold q_norm into wq_b (fusedNorm) and fold Q RoPE into attention (qrope=1),
  dropping separate rms, widen, and Triton _rope launches;
- apply woFold across wo_a -> wo_b and emit bf16 directly from wo_b and
  block_moe so DSpark TP exchanges use direct bf16 all-gather instead of
  exchange_f32's castBf16 + all-gather pair, cutting 23 kernel launches per
  draft round.

Includes a host emission regression test in block_test.zig that fails on
unpatched main. Verified 20/20 greedy replay SHA-256 bit-exact (15,813 tokens)
on 2x GB10 TP=2.
